[{:seon.task/name "the-screen-is-evals"
  :seon.task/plan "Step 2 of notes/design-agent-view-2026-10-24.md (approved, docs/decisions.md 2026-10-24). The screen is evals: `seon.screen/forms` (`(my.task/status)`, `(my.branch/changes)`) are evaluated in the agent's REPL just before each model request (`seon.turn/act!`), each recorded by the screen (:seon.eval/by \"screen\"), named by the turn's basis (:screen) and sent as the request's last user messages {:by \"screen\" :code .. :response ..} (the eval fact's :seon.render/ai, `seon.context/eval-messages`), replaced each request. The agent's page joins the screen as a read of root's cached view (design section 10, step 4; the prototype's hand-built `seon.screen/show` was deleted in step 1, seon.render/a-page-part-renders-only-its-view). The printer's two general changes: a sequence fills breadth before depth as a map does (`seon.print.select/fill-members`), and a value an earlier response showed prints as the form that reads it again (`:seen`, built by `seon.repl/printed`'s caller). Replaces: the screen's turn sections in one text (`seon.context/screen-message`, kept for an outside agent's read); `seon.context/current-state` splits into `run-state` and `turn-state`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.context-test/the-request-is-a-conversation-of-evals-then-the-screen
                      seon.print-test/members-fill-breadth-before-depth
                      seon.print-test/an-earlier-value-prints-as-its-handle}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-screen-is-sent-as-diffs"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner's ruling (docs/decisions.md, the screen is sent as diffs between turns, 2026-10-25): `(seon.screen/show {:since t})` answers what changed since the agent's last screen at db t, the unchanged sections named; the first screen of a run is whole; a section about to be cut by the history budget is sent whole again. Design: notes/design-agent-loop-2026-10-25.md section 5 (on jolt/agent-loop). Measured need (the live-agents session, 2026-10-25): the screen is 1.2-1.8k tokens a turn, more than the story, and sent uncached every request, because `seon.context/request` sends the turn's screen evals as its last messages and replaces them the next request (`seon.context/records` leaves screen evals out). The change: screen evals are records like any eval, appended in tx order, so the conversation is append-only and the provider's prefix cache holds; `seon.context/printed-run` prints a screen eval against the previous screen eval of the same code as `seon.screen/diff` of the two ({:changed {k v} :unchanged [k ...]}, :since its handle), the mechanism that already prints an equal earlier value as the form that reads it there (`seon.context/fold-of`); `seon.context/as-sent` sends it whole while its base is not sent whole (the ruling's cut rule). Deletes: request's separate screen tail (screen-parts). Measure: the uncached tokens a request adds past the previous request's messages, before and after, on recorded live runs."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.screen-test/a-diff-names-what-is-unchanged seon.context-test/an-unchanged-screen-sends-only-its-names seon.context-test/a-screen-whose-base-is-cut-is-sent-whole}}]
